    "perplexity": {
      "description": "8-Tracks is a Pink Floyd compilation that distills the band’s classic 1971–1979 period into eight carefully chosen songs, offering a concise overview of their rise from expansive progressive rock to worldwide superstardom. The sequence includes signature staples such as “Money,” “Wish You Were Here,” “Another Brick in the Wall, Part 2,” “Time,” and “Comfortably Numb,” alongside earlier material like “One Of These Days” and “Wot’s… Uh The Deal.”\n\nIssued by Sony Music/Columbia, the release is aimed both at new listeners seeking an accessible entry point and longtime fans wanting a tightly curated reminder of the band’s most celebrated era. Its inclusion of a full version of “Pigs On The Wing,” previously available only on the 1977 Animals 8-track cartridge, adds a small archival twist that underscores the project’s connection to Pink Floyd’s original 1970s catalogue.",
